From 7df58e594728d5d48e8953da809904dc04d722ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 23:10:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] perf(dsv41): overlap decode KV/indexer-key writes with
 query/index-query on aux_stream

Base: 1107 vLLM patch head 2756478b60b90700b9918b457aeb38657da637b5.

Rationale:
1. In DeepSeek-V4.1 decode on GB10 (48 SMs), the pre-indexer_score region after wq_b and compressor._project_local consists of small kernels (1 to 24 CTAs at M=1..48) separated by serial stream dependencies:
   - KV+Index source layers (Layers 2, 8, 14 with ratio=2; Layer 20 with ratio=1): compressor._finish_project (gather_columns_into) -> gather_partial_state -> compress(write_kv=True) -> _issue_wo_prefetch(after="compressor") -> project_bf16_partials(indexer.wk) -> _write_index_keys -> tl_metadata.pages, followed serially by _index_query (indexer.wq_b + indexer.weights_proj), _rope(q), _index_chunk (indexer_score + indexer_topk), and _shared_decode_metadata (tl_metadata.decode_metadata).
   - Index-only reindex layers (Layers 24, 28, 32, 36 with ratio=1, compressor=None): _rope(q) -> indexer.wq_b -> indexer.weights_proj before _index_chunk.
2. Factor DeepseekCompressor._project(hidden_states) in vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/compressor.py into _project_local(hidden_states) (project_parts + tensor_model_parallel_all_gather) and _finish_project(gathered, rows) (gather_columns_into) so tensor-parallel all_gather remains on the primary stream before forking aux_stream().
3. Carve two disjoint preallocated workspace slices (main_scratch, aux_scratch) inside _build_tilelang_plans via _decode_overlap_workspace_specs(DECODE_CHUNK) and schedule independent decode work across main_stream and aux_stream():
   - On KV+Index source layers: Phase 1 overlaps _index_query (indexer.wq_b + indexer.weights_proj) on aux_stream with compressor._finish_project + compressor._forward_tilelang + _issue_wo_prefetch(after="compressor") + indexer.wk + _write_index_keys + tl_metadata.pages on main_stream. Phase 2 overlaps _rope(q) + _shared_decode_metadata on aux_stream with _index_chunk (indexer_score + indexer_topk) on main_stream before joining for _attend (sparse_mla).
   - On Index-only reindex layers: overlaps _rope(q) + indexer.weights_proj on aux_stream with project_block32_rope_mxfp4_decode(indexer.wq_b) on main_stream before joining for forward_mqa.
   - All cross-stream tensor lifetimes are recorded via record_stream so captured CUDA graphs and eager decode preserve allocator safety.

Quality:
Bit-identical (torch.equal, 0 uint16 diffs, max_abs_diff == 0.0) across all TP4 and TP3 shapes (M = 1..48) and all three indexed layer families, both in eager mode and inside captured CUDA graphs.

Tests:
- pytest tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_attention.py tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_compressor.py tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_compressor_prepare.py tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_l2_schedule.py tests/kernels/test_deepseek_v41_tilelang_pdl.py (127 passed across 2 boots).
- _build_tilelang_plans now reads the layer's compressor and indexer projections (_decode_overlap_workspace_specs); every DeepseekV4Attention sets both (compressor and indexer.wk exist exactly on KV sources). The hand-built layers of tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_lsa.py::test_lsa_opt_in_32k_to_1m_routing_and_metadata_wiring and tests/v1/worker/test_workspace.py::test_v41_tilelang_attention_reserves_scratch_in_its_model_lane now carry them: KV-source layers a compressor and an indexer with wk, wq_b and weights_proj; the window-only drafter neither.

Upstream status: local DeepSeek V4.1 TileLang decode dual-stream attention/compressor/indexer overlap for GB10.
